---
import Brand from "../../components/Brand.astro";
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { config } from "../../config";
import { privacyLine } from "../../data/features";
---
<Legal title="Privacy notice" description="How ola collects, uses and protects personal data (DRAFT, needs legal review).">
  <p><strong>In short:</strong> {privacyLine}</p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    {config.companyName} is the controller of your personal data. Contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${config.supportEmail}`}>{config.supportEmail}</a>.
    {/* TODO(owner): ICO registration number; EU representative (Art. 27 GDPR) if required; DPO if appointed. */}
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account data</strong> (name, email, password hash, country) — to provide your account. Legal basis: contract.</li>
    <li><strong>Order data</strong> (items, amounts, shipping address, tracking) — to deliver your order and meet tax and accounting duties. Legal basis: contract and legal obligation.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment data</strong> — handled by Stripe; we do not store your full card details. Legal basis: contract.</li>
    <li><strong>Voice and conversations</strong> — when you tap the mic, your voice is sent to our servers and to our AI partners (OpenAI) to transcribe it and generate a spoken reply. Transcripts and replies are stored in your conversation history. Legal basis: contract.</li>
    <li><strong>Watch settings and usage</strong> (language, persona, colours, usage amounts for the fair-use allowance). Legal basis: contract.</li>
    <li><strong>Website analytics</strong> — {config.plausibleDomain ? "cookieless, aggregated statistics (Plausible); no personal profiles." : "none at present."} Legal basis: legitimate interests.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Who we share it with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>OpenAI (AI processing of voice and text) — {/* TODO(owner): confirm DPA, retention settings and transfer mechanism. */} as our processor.</li>
    <li>Stripe (payments and billing).</li>
    <li>Our hosting provider and email provider. {/* TODO(owner): name them. */}</li>
    <li>Delivery carriers (name and address only).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We never sell your data and we don't use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>4. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some providers may process data outside the UK/EEA (for example in the United States). Where they do, we rely on
    appropriate safeguards such as the UK International Data Transfer Addendum / EU Standard Contractual Clauses or an
    adequacy decision. {/* TODO(owner): list per provider. */}
  </p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Conversation history: until you delete it or close your account. Order and tax records: as long as the law requires
    (typically 6–10 years). {/* TODO(owner): confirm retention periods, including at AI partners. */}
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can access, correct, export or delete your data, object to or restrict certain processing, and withdraw consent
    where we rely on it. You can export or delete your conversation history yourself in your account at any time. You
    can complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk) or your local EU data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Children</h2>
  <p>ola is intended for adults. You must be 18 or over to buy an <Brand name="watch" /> and create an account.
    {/* TODO(owner): confirm minimum age policy. */}</p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>Connections between the watch, your ola account and our servers are encrypted. Access to personal data is restricted to people who need it.</p>
</Legal>
